#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""hasler-install - put Hasler on a fresh moOde card, from a SIGNED release.

docs/new-install.md. Nothing it downloads is run before it has been checked:

    pinned root key (below) -> keyring.json(.sig)          namespace hasler-keyring
    keyring timestamp key   -> channels/<channel>.json(.sig) namespace hasler-channel
    index release_sha256    -> release.json, keyring release key -> .sig  hasler-release
    release.json sha256/size -> the tarball -> files.sha256 -> every file

Then it runs the release's own box setup (scripts/bootstrap.sh and
scripts/ota-bootstrap.sh, carried in the release under app/setup/), writes
/etc/hasler/box.yaml, hands moOde its settings (moodecfg.ini, applied by
moOde's worker at the next boot), and lets the release's updater stage and
install the release exactly as it installs every later update.

Commands (root unless noted):

    hasler-install fetch --out DIR [--channel C]   download, verify, unpack, assemble
                                                   the setup tree; changes nothing else
                                                   (any user, any machine)
    hasler-install install [--channel C] [--user U] [--variant V] [--panel-optional]
                   [--no-moode] [--yes]            the SSH path: setup now, then it reboots
                                                   and finishes by itself (hasler-install.service)
    hasler-install resume                          what hasler-install.service runs: the
                                                   next step of an install, after each boot
    hasler-install hook                            cloud-init vendor-data's call on the first
                                                   boot: copy this file and start the service
    hasler-install status                          where an install is (any user)

Common: --base URL (default the public channel), --root-pub FILE (another root
key - bench drills with dev keys), --settings FILE (default
/boot/firmware/hasler.txt, the owner's settings on the SD card).

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 75 not yet (waiting; the service retries).
"""

